      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/learned_mississippi"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was incorporated March 14, 1884, after a post office opened in 1882, and grew along the Yazoo and Mississippi Valley Railroad.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/learned_mississippi"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early commerce in Learned centered on general stores, a cotton gin, and hotels, reflecting the town’s role as a regional trade hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/learned_mississippi"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Learned sits 25 miles southwest of Jackson and 27 miles southeast of Vicksburg, placing it within easy reach of Mississippi’s capital and historic river city.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Learned%2C_Mississippi"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The surrounding landscape is predominantly farmland and woodlands, with no major natural landmarks directly within Learned’s limits.",
